# No-cache the kill-switch — we want every revisit to fetch fresh so the
# SW + HTML stay current as users transition off. Static cache here would
# defeat the purpose since the whole point is to invalidate stale state.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate, max-age=0
  Pragma: no-cache

# Service Worker file: critical it's never cached and always served with
# the right MIME so the browser will treat it as a SW.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate, max-age=0
  Content-Type: application/javascript; charset=utf-8
  Service-Worker-Allowed: /
